//@version=6
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// VWAP Rope Band by Bybllo
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// OVERVIEW
// This indicator plots a smoothed trend line (the "rope") that only
// moves once price has traveled beyond a VWAP-deviation threshold
// from its last position, so small back-and-forth noise around VWAP
// is absorbed and the line only steps in the direction of a genuine
// move. The threshold itself is the standard deviation of (close -
// VWAP) over a lookback period, scaled by a multiplier, so the band
// automatically widens or narrows with how far price is currently
// dispersing from VWAP. A true-direction transition is only
// registered once the rope actually reverses direction (not just on
// every VWAP wiggle), and that short transition window can be marked
// with its own color, an optional cloud, and an optional Buy/Sell
// badge at the exact point the reversal begins.
//
// INTENDED USE - FUTURES SCALPING / LOWER TIMEFRAMES
// This indicator works well for short-term futures scalping (Nasdaq
// futures, KOSPI200 futures, and similar instruments). It is built
// and tuned primarily for the 1-minute chart, but the underlying
// VWAP/rope/band logic is timeframe-agnostic and holds up well on 2,
// 3, and 5-minute charts and other intraday timeframes too - the
// StdDev Length and Band Multiplier will naturally adapt to the
// volatility of whichever timeframe and instrument you're viewing,
// but it's still worth re-checking them when you switch, since what
// counts as a "meaningful" deviation from VWAP on a 1-minute NASDAQ
// chart is not the same as on a 5-minute KOSPI200 chart.
//
// WHY A "ROPE" INSTEAD OF PLOTTING VWAP DIRECTLY
// VWAP itself moves on every single bar, constantly wiggling above
// and below the "true" fair-value area as short-term trades push
// price back and forth. Watching VWAP directly for trend direction
// means reading a lot of that noise as if it were meaningful. The
// rope line in this indicator behaves differently: it only advances
// once price has drifted further than (StdDev of price-vs-VWAP x
// Band Multiplier) away from the rope's current value. Until that
// threshold is crossed, the rope holds perfectly still - it does not
// creep toward VWAP the way a simple moving average would. Every
// step the rope takes therefore represents a statistically
// meaningful deviation from VWAP, not noise, which is what makes its
// color and slope usable as a clean trend read at a glance.
//
// HOW THE BAND ADAPTS TO VOLATILITY
// Unlike a fixed-width band, the upper and lower lines here are
// computed as rope +/- the same VWAP-deviation threshold used to
// move the rope itself. Because that threshold is a rolling standard
// deviation, the band automatically widens when price is currently
// dispersing further from VWAP (higher volatility regime) and
// narrows when price is tracking VWAP closely (lower volatility
// regime) - you don't need to manually adjust the band width as
// conditions change; it self-adjusts every bar.
//
// GRADIENT CLOUD FILL
// The area between the rope and each band is filled using Pine's
// native true-gradient fill() feature: color intensity is strongest
// right at the band edge and fades to fully transparent as it
// approaches the rope line, rather than being a single flat color
// across the whole band width. The "Gradient Steepness" input
// controls how quickly that fade happens - a low value concentrates
// the strong color into a narrow strip right at the band edge (a
// sharp, high-contrast look), while a value near 1.0 spreads the
// color gradually across the entire band (a soft, gentle look).
//
// TRANSITION DETECTION AND THE BUY/SELL SIGNAL BADGE
// The indicator does not flag "direction changed" on every bar the
// rope happens to move - it specifically waits for the rope to move
// in the opposite direction from its last confirmed direction. The
// very first bar that happens is treated as the start of a genuine
// reversal: a short transition window opens (colored separately from
// both the up and down colors), and, if "Buy/Sell Signal" is
// enabled, a BUY or SELL badge is plotted right at that bar - the
// earliest point the reversal is confirmed, rather than only after
// the new trend has fully established itself. If the rope reverses
// back to the original direction while still inside this window, the
// transition simply resolves back to the original trend color. If
// the new direction instead continues, the transition clears and the
// new trend color becomes the established one. As a safety cap, the
// transition window also expires on its own after 5 bars even if
// direction hasn't resolved either way, so the chart never gets
// stuck showing a "transition" state indefinitely.
//
// CHART-TYPE COMPATIBILITY
// Price data (high/low/close, and the source used for the VWAP
// calculation) is pulled via request.security() against the plain
// underlying ticker rather than read directly off the chart, so the
// rope, band, and VWAP values are identical whether your chart is
// displaying candlesticks, Heikin Ashi, Renko, or any other
// non-standard chart type.
//
// ALERTS
// Two independent alert families are provided: simple center-line
// crossover/crossunder alerts (price crossing above/below the rope,
// useful as a lightweight "price vs. VWAP-rope" notification
// regardless of whether a full reversal is confirmed), and Buy/Sell
// Signal alerts tied specifically to the confirmed-transition badges
// described above.
//
// HOW TO USE
// - Treat the rope line's color and slope as the current trend
//   direction relative to VWAP; a color change (through the
//   transition color) signals that a genuine reversal has begun.
// - Use the upper/lower band as a volatility-adjusted VWAP envelope -
//   price pushing into the band without a rope reversal can be read
//   as continuation, while a rope flip suggests the move against VWAP
//   may be running out of steam.
// - Turn on "Buy/Sell Signal" if you want a badge plotted right where
//   a confirmed reversal begins, or turn it off if you only want the
//   line/cloud visuals.
// - Lower "Gradient Steepness" for a shorter, more intense color
//   burst near the band edges, or raise it for a smoother gradient
//   spread across the full band width.
// - Set up alerts on the rope crossover/crossunder conditions for
//   simple VWAP-cross notifications, or on the Buy/Sell signal
//   conditions for confirmed-reversal notifications.
// - Built primarily for 1-minute futures scalping (Nasdaq futures,
//   KOSPI200, and similar), but works well on 2/3/5-minute charts
//   and other intraday timeframes too - just keep an eye on the
//   StdDev Length and Band Multiplier when you switch timeframe or
//   instrument, since what counts as a meaningful VWAP deviation
//   scales with both.
//
// NOTES
// - The gradient fill relies on Pine's built-in fill() gradient
//   feature, which is supported across all account tiers (free and
//   paid).
// - The transition window auto-clears after 5 bars if the rope has
//   not continued in the new direction, so it always reflects a
//   short, recent window rather than an indefinitely "stuck" state.
// - Because ta.vwap() resets at the start of each new session/day by
//   default, the rope's behavior around session opens will reflect
//   that VWAP reset.
//
// DISCLAIMER
// For educational and informational purposes only. This is not
// financial advice. Past performance does not guarantee future
// results. Always verify how the rope and bands behave on your
// specific symbol and timeframe before relying on them for live
// trading.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
indicator("VWAP Rope Band by Bybllo", overlay = true)
// ═══════════════════════════════
// INPUTS
// ═══════════════════════════════
var g1 = "Parameters"
multi = input.float(1.75, "Band Multiplier", step = 0.25, minval = 0.25, group = g1)
len   = input.int(23,    "StdDev Length",   minval = 1,  group = g1)
var g2 = "Display"
show_cloud        = input.bool(true, "Show Transition Cloud", group = g2)
show_gradient     = input.bool(true, "Show Gradient Cloud",   group = g2)
grad_steepness    = input.float(0.2, "Gradient Steepness", minval = 0.05, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.05, group = g2, tooltip = "Lower values concentrate the color intensity closer to the edges over a short distance, creating a steeper gradient (1.0 = a gentle gradient spread across the full width)")
show_trade_signal = input.bool(true, "Buy/Sell Signal", group = g2, tooltip = "Displays a Buy/Sell badge at the point where the Transition Cloud begins")
var g3 = "Colors"
up_col       = input.color(color.yellow,           "Up",             group = g3)
dn_col       = input.color(#067814,          "Down",           group = g3)
fl_col       = input.color(#ff0000,                "Transition",     group = g3)
cld_col      = input.color(color.new(#1848cc, 80), "Cloud",          group = g3)
up_cloud_col = input.color(color.new(#e65100, 50), "Up Cloud Color", group = g3)
dn_cloud_col = input.color(color.new(#00591F, 50), "Down Cloud Color", group = g3)
up_line_col  = input.color(color.new(#ffeb4b, 30), "Up Line Color",  group = g3)
dn_line_col  = input.color(color.new(#049457, 30), "Down Line Color", group = g3)
// ═══════════════════════════════
// Force real market prices regardless of chart type (Heikin Ashi,
// Renko, etc.) via request.security (the internal source used by
// ta.vwap must also be swapped for real prices)
// ═══════════════════════════════
t = ticker.new(syminfo.prefix, syminfo.ticker)
[rh, rl, rc] = request.security(t, timeframe.period, [high, low, close])
real_hlc3 = (rh + rl + rc) / 3
// ═══════════════════════════════
// VWAP THRESHOLD
// ═══════════════════════════════
vwap_val  = ta.vwap(real_hlc3)
threshold = ta.stdev(rc - vwap_val, len) * multi
// ═══════════════════════════════
// ROPE SMOOTHER
// ═══════════════════════════════
var float rope = rc
rope += math.max(math.abs(rc - rope) - nz(threshold, 0), 0) * math.sign(rc - rope)
upper = rope + threshold
lower = rope - threshold
// @function     Draws a Buy (Long) / Sell (Short) badge (at the point where the Transition Cloud begins)
// @param bullish true = Buy badge (Up color = yellow, below the candle), false = Sell badge (Down Line Color = green, above the candle)
// @returns      void
drawTradeSignal(bool bullish) =>
    if bullish
        label.new(chart.point.new(time, na, rl), 'BUY', xloc.bar_time, yloc = yloc.belowbar, color = color.new(up_col, 0), textcolor = color.black, style = label.style_label_up, size = size.small)
    else
        label.new(chart.point.new(time, na, rh), 'SELL', xloc.bar_time, yloc = yloc.abovebar, color = color.new(dn_line_col, 0), textcolor = color.black, style = label.style_label_down, size = size.small)
// ═══════════════════════════════
// CORE LOGIC:
// last_real_dir = the last direction the rope actually moved in (1 or -1)
// A transition is only registered once real movement is confirmed in
// the opposite direction
// ═══════════════════════════════
var int  last_real_dir = 0
var bool in_transition = false
rope_moved = rope != rope[1]
buySignal  = false
sellSignal = false
if rope_moved
    new_dir = rope > rope[1] ? 1 : -1
    // The first time movement occurs opposite to last_real_dir = a genuine reversal (the Transition Cloud's starting point)
    if last_real_dir != 0 and new_dir != last_real_dir
        in_transition := true
        if show_trade_signal
            drawTradeSignal(new_dir == 1)
        buySignal  := new_dir == 1
        sellSignal := new_dir == -1
    // The transition ends once movement resumes in the new direction after the reversal
    if in_transition and new_dir == last_real_dir * -1
        true
    else if in_transition and new_dir == last_real_dir
        in_transition := false
    last_real_dir := new_dir
// Auto-end the transition window if it runs on too long (5 bars)
var int trans_bars = 0
if in_transition
    trans_bars += 1
    if trans_bars > 5
        in_transition := false
        trans_bars    := 0
else
    trans_bars := 0
col = in_transition ? fl_col : last_real_dir == 1 ? up_col : last_real_dir == -1 ? dn_col : up_col
// ═══════════════════════════════
// Detect price crossing above / below the center line (rope)
// ═══════════════════════════════
crossUp   = ta.crossover( rc, rope)  // close price crosses above the center line
crossDown = ta.crossunder(rc, rope)  // close price crosses below the center line
// ═══════════════════════════════
// PLOTS
// ═══════════════════════════════
mid_is_bullish = not in_transition and last_real_dir == 1
whole_line_col = mid_is_bullish ? up_line_col : dn_line_col
p_mid   = plot(rope,  "Rope",  color = col,            linewidth = 3)
p_upper = plot(upper, "Upper", color = whole_line_col, linewidth = 1)
p_lower = plot(lower, "Lower", color = whole_line_col, linewidth = 1)
// ═══════════════════════════════
// GRADIENT
// ═══════════════════════════════
whole_cloud_col = mid_is_bullish ? up_cloud_col : dn_cloud_col
whole_fade_col  = color.new(whole_cloud_col, 100)
up_fade_point = upper - (upper - rope) * grad_steepness
dn_fade_point = lower + (rope  - lower) * grad_steepness
fill(p_upper, p_mid, upper, up_fade_point, show_gradient ? whole_cloud_col : na, show_gradient ? whole_fade_col : na, title = "Upper Gradient")
fill(p_mid, p_lower, dn_fade_point, lower, show_gradient ? whole_fade_col : na, show_gradient ? whole_cloud_col : na, title = "Lower Gradient")
// ═══════════════════════════════
// TRANSITION ZONE CLOUD
// ═══════════════════════════════
hu = plot(upper, color = in_transition and show_cloud ? color.new(fl_col, 100) : na, editable = false)
hl = plot(lower, color = in_transition and show_cloud ? color.new(fl_col, 100) : na, editable = false)
fill(hu, hl, in_transition and show_cloud ? cld_col : na, title = "Transition Cloud")
// ═══════════════════════════════
// ALERTS
// ═══════════════════════════════
alertcondition(crossUp,    "Cross Above (Center Line)", "Cross Above (Center Line) - VWAP Rope Band by Bybllo")
alertcondition(crossDown,  "Cross Below (Center Line)", "Cross Below (Center Line) - VWAP Rope Band by Bybllo")
alertcondition(buySignal,  "Buy Signal",  "Buy Signal - VWAP Rope Band by Bybllo")
alertcondition(sellSignal, "Sell Signal", "Sell Signal - VWAP Rope Band by Bybllo")
//-------------------------------------------------------------------}
